            <ArticleTitle>[Computed tomography of the heart].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1275-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Noninvasive evaluation of the coronary arteries by multi-detector row computed tomography is a promising new alternative to conventional invasive coronary angiography. This article describes the technical background, methods, limitations and clinical applications and reviews current literature that compares the diagnostic accuracy of multi-detector row computed tomography with that of coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
